@module patrollers ; The three patrollers: guards that walk a row through several rooms
@about A patroller walks along a row of the world, a column every four of its turns (one turn every three passes), from room to room; it turns where its record says. It is drawn only when it is in the droid's room. Its mark 8 in the cells kills the droid at a touch (HazardDeath).

$93A6 c MovePatroller ; One turn of the patroller at PatrollerPtr: erase, step, draw
> Erase it (DrawPatroller) when it was drawn and is in the room; clear bit 7; PatrollerStep; draw it when it is in the room. L1 18 583 turns, 495 erased, 507 drawn.
$93C1 MovePatrollerStep

$93E0 c PatrollerStep ; Advance the frame; every fourth a column, round the ends
> +0 the frame 0-3; at 4: a column right (y bit 0 clear) or left; past column $1C (or below 0) into the next room (+3 + 1 or - 1) at column 0 (or $1C); at the right end (room +4, column +5) or the left end (+6, +7) it turns (bit 0 of y flips) and steps back. L1 18 583, 4 630 steps, 102 + 72 room changes, 28 + 28 turns.
$93F8 PatrollerStepRightEnd
$940A PatrollerStepLeft
$9417 PatrollerStepLeftEnd

$942D c DrawPatroller ; XOR a patroller into the sprite list and its mark into the cells
> The frame from $B902 (walking right) or $BA82 (left), 96 bytes a frame (4 bytes x 24 rows: Patrol graphics); 4 x 3 character cells, the mark DrawMode (8), the attribute $42. L1 1 002.
$943C DrawPatrollerColumn
$9446 DrawPatrollerFrame
$944A DrawPatrollerQueue

$9484 b StartPositions 2 ; Where the droid starts in each of the 128 rooms: (x, y)
> PlaceDroid $7A7B reads StartPositions + 2 x Room after a life lost and at a new game (room $54). The editable form is part of src/res/rooms/ (the start of each room).
@res rooms/StartPositions.bin

@module interrupt ; The IM 2 set-up and the interrupt handler: the sprites, the controls, the scroller
$9584 c SetupIM2 ; The IM 2 table, the empty sprite list, the scroller reset, the handler installed
> 257 bytes of $5B at Im2Table ($FE00-$FF00), so the vector is $5B5B whatever the bus holds; JP Interrupt at $5B5B; I = $FE; IM 2. L1 1 (c1).
$958A SetupIM2Table

$95C1 b ExitToBasic 8 ; Never run: LD A,$3F; LD I,A; IM 1; EI; CALL $0D6B (CLS); LD A,7; OUT ($FE),A; RET
> The way back to BASIC that no code reaches (L1: no run, no read): the I register and IM 1 restored, the screen cleared, the border white. A leftover of development.

$95D0 c Interrupt ; Every frame: read the controls, XOR the sprite list, scroll the message, the timers, the ROM keyboard
> Saves the registers; ReadControls; then each sprite list record from SpriteListEnd (graphic, flag pointer, width, rows / 8, screen address): its rows are XORed onto the screen and, when a byte of the sprite falls on ink already there ((screen AND sprite) is not 0), bit 7 of the flag byte is set (InterruptCollide: L1 35 639 of 68 835 sprites). Then the scroller, every ScrollDelay frames (5; 15 after a whole text row): the 19-byte window at $402C (31 pixel lines) moves up one pixel line and the next pixel row of 19 characters comes in at the bottom (ScrollScreen): row ScrollLine - 1 of each glyph, Font - 1 + 8 x code + ScrollLine. After 8 lines the text moves on 19 characters; at a '.' the queued message (ScrollNext) starts, or none. Then WeaponSelect, EnergyTick, DrainTimer, the ROM's KEYBOARD (FRAMES and LAST_K), the registers back, EI, RETI.
> Witness: L1 54 811 interrupts; 123 658 list reads; the scroller 8 773 steps.
$95DB InterruptSprite
$9609 InterruptSpriteRow
$960E InterruptSpriteByte
$9619 InterruptSpriteNext
